  "behavior": [
    "Explicit opt-in RootSpace::ReferenceWorld requires a declared single physical hierarchy root. Its author transform is already global and is copied without applying placement R/T again. Descendants compose with observed Single precision. Placement scale still participates in existing physical-scale admission; this does not widen admitted graph policies.",
    "Default ObjectLocal behavior and Double precision remain unchanged. ReferenceWorld dynamic snapshot writeback has no synthetic native parent at the root and uses Single precision for children. Checkpoint capture and restore retain controller locals.",
    "Shared MatrixTransform::getControllerTransform preserves separately cached NIF rotation bits when the scaled drawing matrix agrees. Raw procedural controller matrices can reconstruct rotation if the cache is stale. It reads author state independently of traversal projection handles. NifSceneTraversal now uses this same reader.",
    "No production caller selects ReferenceWorld in this checkpoint. ObjectAnimation retains its current local-root binding and World retains root-only inverse-bind synchronization. This adapter alone cannot establish native attachment or live manual traversal."
  ],
